==English==

=== Etymology 1 ===

==== Etymology ====
1923 {{term|mike}}, 1961 ''mic''. Abbreviation and alteration of {{term|microphone}}. The earlier version is probably influenced by speech, and the later by abbreviations on recording equipment.

==== Alternative forms ====
* ''[[mike]]''

==== Pronunciation ====
* {{IPA|/ˈmaɪk/}}

==== Noun ====
{{en-noun}}

# [[microphone|Microphone]].

==== Verb ====
{{en-verb|mikes|miking|miked}}

# {{transitive|and|intransitive}} To put one or microphones on or in; to use or place a microphone.
#: ''If we add the drum kit, we'll have to '''mic''' the orchestra.''

==== References ====
* '''2010''', “[http://www.nytimes.com/2010/08/01/magazine/01-onlanguage-t.html?_r=1&partner=rssnyt&emc=rss On Language: How Should ‘Microphone’ be Abbreviated?]”, in ''New York Times'', July 29.

